  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Implemented canonical typed uint64 &, |, ^, <<, and >> operations across exact, binary64, and source-transparent prime IR plus portable JavaScript, isolated C, word, tagged, and prime-source backends. Augmented scalar and UInt64Buffer lowering preserves Python target-before-RHS evaluation order, uses explicit 0..63 shift guards, logical right shift, and modulo-2^64 left shift. Sage-mode native-bitwise source now preserves xor and uses checked full-word dynamic helpers for mixed exact Number/BigInt values rather than JavaScript 32-bit operators. Prime-source Node returns preserve the full unsigned range as BigInt, exposed JavaScript fallbacks validate the public ABI, and adversarial tests cover 2^40, 2^63, 2^64-1, invalid operands, shift 64, mixed representations, dynamic fallback, native C, and portable JavaScript. IR v22, cache fingerprinting, explain metadata, host/policy benchmark metadata, compiler documentation, and Node test-manifest registration are included.",
    "risks": [
      "The fresh required pnpm test:compiler receipt at commit 3e0ef0d passed 14/15 runnable fixtures and failed only compiler/matrix.py: sample_sparse_random_spec reaches sorted/list and raises TypeError: object is not iterable under Node 26.7.0. That sparse-random path is outside every claim in this lane; compiler/algebra.py passed in 43 seconds.",
      "The required broad integration tier was not rerun after the unchanged matrix blocker, per coordinator direction not to broaden this lane into matrix remediation. Its earlier receipt passed 371/380 tests and failed eight matrix/polynomial runtime tests outside this claim; fresh focused dynamic/portable/native, native-kernel, frontend/operator, build, architecture, and strict receipts pass.",
      "CPython's annotation-only uint64 fallback retains Python int left-shift behavior; full-word wrapping and 0..63 guards are the documented typed-IR/native/portable-JavaScript contract, so a CPython oracle that reaches overflow or an out-of-range shift must make that boundary explicit."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Integration lane: apply the exact src/lib/sagejs/native.py documentation patch supplied separately to the coordinator; it updates Native Kernel v21 to v22 and documents the full-word operators, augmented forms, wrapping/logical shifts, count validation, dynamic Sage.js semantics, and CPython annotation-only difference.",
      "Integration lane: rerun pnpm test:compiler and pnpm test:integration after rebasing onto the current integration base and preparing its native cache; investigate only if the recorded unrelated matrix/polynomial failures remain.",
      "The test manifest follow-up is already complete in this lane: test/native-uint64-bitwise.cjs is registered in test/node-test-manifest.cjs."
    ]
  }
